### ==========================================
### MS-BANCARIO - Ejemplos de peticiones HTTP
### ==========================================
### Archivo compatible con IntelliJ HTTP Client
### También puedes importar estos ejemplos a Postman
### ==========================================

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:9595
@contentType = application/json

### ==========================================
### 1. AUTENTICACIÓN
### ==========================================

### 1.1 Registrar nuevo usuario
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "USER"
}

### 1.2 Login (obtener tokens)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 1.3 Login con usuario normal
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "user1",
  "password": "user123"
}

### 1.4 Refrescar token
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### ==========================================
### 2. GESTIÓN DE CLIENTES (Requiere autenticación)
### ==========================================

### 2.1 Crear cliente (requiere rol ADMIN o USER)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "nombre": "Pedro González",
  "email": "pedro.gonzalez@example.com"
}

### 2.2 Crear cliente con validaciones fallidas (debe dar error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "nombre": "Pe",
  "email": "email-invalido"
}

### 2.3 Crear cliente con email duplicado (debe dar error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "nombre": "Juan Pérez",
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com"
}

### ==========================================
### 3. PRUEBAS DE SEGURIDAD
### ==========================================

### 3.1 Intentar acceder sin token (debe dar 403/401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "nombre": "Sin autenticación",
  "email": "sin.auth@example.com"
}

### 3.2 Intentar acceder con token inválido (debe dar 403/401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer token_invalido_12345

{
  "nombre": "Token inválido",
  "email": "token.invalido@example.com"
}

### 3.3 Intentar acceder con token expirado (debe dar 403/401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ0ZXN0IiwiaWF0IjoxNjAwMDAwMDAwLCJleHAiOjE2MDAwMDAwMDB9.xyz

{
  "nombre": "Token expirado",
  "email": "token.expirado@example.com"
}

### ==========================================
### 4. EJEMPLOS CON CURL (PowerShell)
### ==========================================

### 4.1 Login con curl
# curl -X POST http://localhost:9595/v1/auth/login `
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" `
#   -d '{"username":"admin","password":"admin123"}'

### 4.2 Crear cliente con curl
# $token = "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs..."  # Reemplazar con token real
# curl -X POST http://localhost:9595/v1/clientes `
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" `
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $token" `
#   -d '{"nombre":"Juan Pérez","email":"juan@example.com"}'

### ==========================================
### NOTAS:
### ==========================================
### - Los tokens se guardan automáticamente en variables globales
### - Reemplaza {{accessToken}} con tu token real si es necesario
### - Los endpoints de /v1/clientes solo son accesibles con rol ADMIN o USER
### - El token expira en 1 hora (3600000 ms)
### - El refresh token expira en 1 día (86400000 ms)
### ==========================================

